{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}

{% block content %}
<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pt-24 pb-12 text-center">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500">Private component exchange</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Publish once.<br>Run everywhere your team works.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        Forest packages typed automation and developer tools as one versioned component.
        Lock it in repositories, invoke it in CI, or install its verified tool directly on your workstation.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="mailto:contact@kjuulh.io?subject=Forest%20private%20preview" class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-md text-sm font-medium hover:bg-gray-800">Join the waitlist</a>
        <a href="/pricing" class="px-5 py-2.5 border border-gray-300 rounded-md text-sm font-medium hover:border-gray-400">See pricing strategy</a>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    {# `code-surface` keeps this block dark in both light and dark mode. #}
    <div class="code-surface rounded-lg p-6 text-sm font-mono overflow-x-auto">
        <pre><span class="text-gray-500"># One versioned capability in a repository</span>
<span class="text-green-400">$</span> forest add acme/policy-check@1.4.0
<span class="text-green-400">$</span> forest validate
<span class="text-green-400">$</span> forest run check --policy production

<span class="text-gray-500"># The same private catalogue on a workstation</span>
<span class="text-green-400">$</span> forest global add acme/devctl@2.1.0
<span class="text-green-400">$</span> devctl release status</pre>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-center text-sm text-gray-500">
        CUE contracts make inputs inspectable. Lock files and checksums make resolution reproducible.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-12">A distribution contract for platform capabilities</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div class="p-6 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Typed components</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
                Define commands, inputs, outputs, and configuration in CUE. Generate SDK bindings and catch invalid configuration before execution.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Private, versioned artifacts</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
                Publish per-platform artifacts to an organisation catalogue. Consumers resolve intentional versions into a checked-in lock file.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Repository and workstation</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
                Use the same component through <code>forest run</code> in CI and through a lazily installed <code>forest global</code> tool on developer machines.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="p-6 border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 rounded-lg">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-lg">Private preview: trusted components only</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
            Forest is currently suitable only for trusted internal evaluation on a private network. Native components run with the invoking user's privileges, global-tool warming may persist publisher-controlled shell code, and runner/artifact authorization is not ready for mutually untrusted tenants. Sandboxing, workload identity, permanent coordinates, provenance, and scanning are launch gates—not features we pretend already exist.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
